{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01073",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.32,
      "end_seconds": 5.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I've settled them in, ready when you are."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.88,
      "end_seconds": 12.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.86,
      "end_seconds": 21.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Well, I wanted to get I can't get my breath looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.06,
      "end_seconds": 27.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.37,
      "end_seconds": 32.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "mm, ever since... since this morning, really"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.24,
      "end_seconds": 43.57,
      "duration_seconds": 10.33,
      "text": "tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.41,
      "end_seconds": 72.74,
      "duration_seconds": 27.33,
      "text": "Actually, um, it's on and off. Mostly moderate. It settles a little with sitting up. I told my wife I'd come today. And there's wheezing as well, about a month now. With wheezing, moderate, I'd say. Not being able to finish a sentence was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.02,
      "end_seconds": 80.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Have you had you can't get your breath before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.17,
      "end_seconds": 90.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened a couple of years ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.03,
      "end_seconds": 99.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "have you had any chest pain, fever or blue tinge?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.75,
      "end_seconds": 106.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "no, uh, no chest pain, fever or blue tinge"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.51,
      "end_seconds": 109.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.75,
      "end_seconds": 114.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Uh, nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.81,
      "end_seconds": 118.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.8,
      "end_seconds": 120.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.36,
      "end_seconds": 125.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Alright, have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.16,
      "end_seconds": 131.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "I had a triple bypass eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.74,
      "end_seconds": 135.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "So, what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.46,
      "end_seconds": 142.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "I've, I've got asthma i've got thin bones"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.03,
      "end_seconds": 144.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.23,
      "end_seconds": 150.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "mm, um, I've had heart disease, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.07,
      "end_seconds": 154.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "tell me your medicines, please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.05,
      "end_seconds": 160.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Uh, I'm on Seretide inhaler, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.59,
      "end_seconds": 162.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "I see, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.89,
      "end_seconds": 178.58,
      "duration_seconds": 14.69,
      "text": "I'm on alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week for my bones. It's clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day. A blue reliever inhaler, 100 micrograms, maybe, every few minutes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.26,
      "end_seconds": 186.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.72,
      "end_seconds": 190.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "No, it's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.21,
      "end_seconds": 193.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.95,
      "end_seconds": 198.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.65,
      "end_seconds": 206.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.56,
      "end_seconds": 211.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.42,
      "end_seconds": 226.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "okay, any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.48,
      "end_seconds": 231.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "um, my cousin has psoriasis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 244.97,
      "end_seconds": 258.97,
      "duration_seconds": 14.0,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Respiratory rate 21, weight 85 kilos, blood pressure 141 over 82. Height 168 centimetres, temperature 37.2, SpO2 93 percent on room air, pulse is 98 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.84,
      "end_seconds": 261.54,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.73,
      "end_seconds": 265.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.59,
      "end_seconds": 267.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.98,
      "end_seconds": 287.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "You are using your neck muscles to breathe, and your oxygen is low."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.35,
      "end_seconds": 301.98,
      "duration_seconds": 10.63,
      "text": "okay, that's enough for me. Having listened and examined, I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at a severe asthma attack or a chest infection"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.68,
      "end_seconds": 306.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Mm, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.0,
      "end_seconds": 318.22,
      "duration_seconds": 10.22,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a severe asthma attack, and we'll know more once the a chest X-ray is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.88,
      "end_seconds": 341.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "A chest X-ray is what I'd like next, for severe breathlessness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.27,
      "end_seconds": 346.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.33,
      "end_seconds": 381.39,
      "duration_seconds": 34.06,
      "text": "the treatment will be prednisolone, 40 milligrams, once now, single dose. You take it by mouth. That's for asthma attack. Sit upright and take slow breaths while the nebuliser is set up. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait. Let's plan a check straight away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.19,
      "end_seconds": 388.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.01,
      "end_seconds": 394.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Mm, um, good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.73,
      "end_seconds": 396.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}